R=[row('opening and complement formula',r'Mod_f/Modf(L); \deleted{\unsure{s|x}}t∈L; \deleted{\unsure{S∪{t}}}; tot. ord',r'Modf(cal L); t∈cal L; no internal deletions; tot. ord.',r'Modf(cal L); \deleted{\unsure{s|x}}t∈cal L; \deleted{\unsure{S∪{t}}}; tot. ord','The f is full height, Ls have looped bases, and two cancellations remain within the set builder. The left cancelled glyph is a dark overwritten blob; the other retains the S, union and brace outlines. No final point follows ord.','011_top.jpg','deletion state','medium'),row('quoted phrase and following connector',r'``composantes connexes’’ un C(S) \unsure{où|à|.}',r'« composantes connexes » un C(S),',r'``composantes connexes’’ un C(S) \unsure{où|à|.}','Two short high quote strokes occur at both ends, not angled guillemets. The last connector is cut by the right edge and remains unresolved.','011_top.jpg','other','medium',C=False),row('first subscripts in enumeration and components',r's_{\deleted{\unsure{0}}1} in four places',r's₁ throughout',r's_{\unsure{p|1|0}} in four places','The small subscript has a p-like closed head and descending stroke, sometimes thickly retraced. There is no securely separable deleted 0 and live 1, so the revision layer asserted by C is replaced by an explicit glyph doubt.','011_top.jpg / 011_components.jpg','math glyph or index','medium'),row('enumeration punctuation',r's₁<s₂,<⋯; ens',r's₁<s₂<⋯; ens.',r's₁<s₂,<⋯; ens','A small comma is visible after s₂ before the next inequality; there is no point after ens.','011_top.jpg / 011_components.jpg','other',C=False),row('component interval list',r'L_{<s₁}, \deleted{\unsure{L}}[s₁,s₂],..., [s_{n−1},s_n], L_{>s_n}',r'cal L_{<s₁}, [s₁,s₂],..., [s_{n−1},s_n], cal L_{>s_n}',r'cal L_{<s_?}, \deleted{\unsure{L}}[s_?,s₂],..., [s_{n−1},s_n], cal L_{>s_n}','Both end Ls have looped feet. The first left bracket is heavily retraced over a possible L, while the last internal pair has clear square brackets facing inward. These surprising closed brackets are retained.','011_components.jpg','deletion state','medium'),row('bracketed cases',r'\unsure{cas|en} n=1; \deleted{\unsure{une}}; voir \unsure{la|le|ce} \unsure{suite|suit} plus haut',r'cas n=1; \struck{une}; voir ce \uncertain{qui est} plus \uncertain{haut}',r'\unsure{en|cas} n=1; \deleted{\unsure{une}}; voir \unsure{la|le|ce} \unsure{suite|suit} plus haut','The n=1 lead-in is a short wave rather than a clearly formed cas. At n≥2 the word after the article has an s, long u/i run and tall t; no separate qui est can be seen. The crossed une remains uncertain.','011_cases.jpg','misread word','medium',marked=True),row('extreme-component sentence',r'les seules non vides \unsure{éventuelles} étant ... \inserted{si} ... \unsure{plus grd}',r'\ill{} non vides \uncertain{intervalles} étant les seules \ill{} ... si ... plus grand',r'les seules non vides éventuelles étant ... \inserted{si} ... plus grd','Les seules opens the line; éventuelles has its two tall l strokes. Both si words sit above the line with leaders, and grd is abbreviated. The written non vides is retained even though the surrounding cases suggest a problem.','011_extremes.jpg','readable ink left as \\ill{}','high',marked=True),row('left boundary cancellations',r'three cancelled fragments by {s₁}, two underbrackets',r'note about a biffed surcharge; underbraces',r'three cancelled fragments by {s₁}, two underbrackets','The upper fragment is s₁-like, the middle retains traces consistent with donc/∅ and the bottom is scribbled over. Squared shallow brackets, with si comp. existe below, are reproduced rather than described.','011_borders.jpg','drawing or diagram','low',C=False),row('recovery assertion',r'structure \unsure{dé|de} \deleted{\unsure{ordr|ordre}} biordre ... \unsure{les structures|la structure}',r'structure \struck{\ill{}} binaire ... la structure',r'structure dé \deleted{\unsure{ordr|ordre}} biordre ... la structure','A separate acute is above the e of dé. The cancelled word begins ord with a tall d; the live word has b-i-o-r-d-r-e. The parenthesis uses singular la structure.','011_bottom.jpg','misread word'),row('circled labels and final S₀',r'circled a \unsure{.} b c; \unsure{scr S|S}_0',r'(a) (b) (c); frak S₀',r'circled a . b c; \unsure{scr S|S}_0','Each label is enclosed by one pen circle, and a point stands between the first two. The final S has a large upper loop and remains doubtful between a flourish and a script form.','011_bottom.jpg','drawing or diagram','medium'),row('watermark','omitted','omitted',r'\unsure{ng Extra Stro}','Pale reverse outline letters run vertically; clipping and handwriting interference leave the whole partial string at low confidence.','011_watermark.jpg / 011_watermark_reading.jpg','omission','low')]
R[2]['consequential']='The first subscripts are recorded as unresolved p/1/0 glyphs, without inventing a cancelled 0 layer.'
R[8]['consequential']='The recovered structure is called biordre, not binaire.'
save(11,t,R,[('text','top','Si S∈Modf(L), on a donc'),('display','top','C(S) set-builder'),('text','upper third','On a dit comment on décomposait'),('display','upper third','S={s_?,...,s_n}'),('text','middle','Les comp. connexes sont les ens'),('display','middle','component interval list'),('display','middle','bracketed n=0, n=1, n≥2 cases'),('text','lower middle','les seules non vides éventuelles'),('display','lower third','component boundaries and squared underbrackets'),('text','bottom','Je dis que l’on récupère'),('text','paper background','ng Extra Stro')],['Modf resolved; overwritten s/x and cancelled S∪{t} retained; connector after C(S) retained.','All four first-subscript 0-deletion doubts are now a single p/1/0 glyph doubt, because no separate cancellation layer is secure. Possible cancelled L before the bracket retained.','For n=1, en is the leading uncertain reading; une and la/le/ce suite/suit remain uncertain.','Éventuelles and plus grd resolved, without repairing non vides. Three cancelled boundary fragments remain uncertain.','Dé, singular la structure and intervening point resolved; cancelled ordr/ordre and script/plain S retained. Watermark newly included with low confidence.'],'Full page and both halves read; six enlarged regions cover every formula, index, cancellation and disputed clause. All closed interval brackets and the anomalous non vides wording were deliberately retained.')
